# CO-CHANAKYA-RELEASE-FREEZE-015 — Hostinger Production Freeze

Status: **ACTIVE** · Product Owner release instruction  
Docs: `docs/co-chanakya-release-freeze-015/CO-CHANAKYA-RELEASE-FREEZE-015.md`

## Hard rule

**Hostinger production is FROZEN for Chanakya-related (and all Chanakya cutover) work.**

`BUILD PASS ≠ PRODUCTION PASS` · `LOCAL PASS ≠ PRODUCTION PASS` · `COMMIT ≠ DEPLOY` · `PUSH ≠ DEPLOY`

Only **explicit Product Owner approval** of the **FINAL CUTOVER** authorises Hostinger production deployment.

## Forbidden until FINAL CUTOVER approval

Do **NOT**:

- deploy to Hostinger / trigger Hostinger production deployment  
- run `prisma migrate deploy` against production  
- change Hostinger production environment variables  
- modify production database schema or production data  
- re-upload production documents  
- perform production cutover  

Passing TypeScript, build, BAT, unit tests, verification scripts, or local checks does **not** authorise production deployment.

## Allowed (development / refinement mode)

- Local implementation and verification  
- Git commit / push to the designated branch **when the Product Owner asks** (or per sprint Git discipline)  
- Continue Chanakya refinement sprints (read-context, OAuth, Opportunity 360, document intelligence, credit proposal, Accounting intelligence, etc.)  
- Keep unrelated dirty/untracked work **out** of Chanakya commits  

## Final cutover (STOP before deploy)

When PO confirms planned Chanakya sprints are complete: freeze feature tree → full verify / tsc / build / BAT / regression-prevention → clean SHA + diff review → env / migrations / OAuth / Credit / Accounting readiness → **FINAL CUTOVER READINESS REPORT** → **STOP**.

Deploy **only** after explicit PO FINAL CUTOVER approval, and **only** the certified clean Git SHA. Validate in production **after** deploy. On failure: **STOP**, diagnose, report — no speculative production fixes / no unapproved rollback.

## Agent behaviour (mandatory)

1. Acknowledge this freeze in **every subsequent Chanakya sprint report**.  
2. Never propose or execute Hostinger deploy / prod migrate / prod env changes for Chanakya work without a separate explicit PO deploy instruction.  
3. Prefer local + Git only until FINAL CUTOVER is approved.

